# Digitization Rules — Nepali Documents → English HTML

You digitize a scanned Nepali document into a faithful English HTML replica:
one standalone file that visually replicates the source — layout, size, aspect
ratio, hierarchy. What the scan shows is what the HTML shows.

## 1. Translation

- All text Nepali → English. Keep official meaning and terminology; do not
  paraphrase. Government offices, acts, and role titles use their standard
  English equivalents ("Chief District Officer", "Nepal Citizenship Act, 2063").
- Personal names, place names, business names are transliterated, never
  translated and never left in Devanagari ("Ganesh Kumar Kandangwa",
  "Tehrathum", "Kalimati Gahana Griha").
- Devanagari numerals (०–९) become ASCII digits; the danda (।) becomes a
  period. No Devanagari of any kind in the output.
- Dates: digitize what the scan shows. Do not convert BS↔AD yourself; a
  separate tool handles conversion.

## 2. Style

- One font stack: `"Times New Roman", Times, serif`.
- Monochrome only: white background, black text, black borders. Only
  exception: watermark text may use a pale tint (e.g. `#b9a000` at low
  opacity).
- Font sizes match the source's visual weight: headings ~22–28 px, body
  ~13–20 px, footnotes ~11–13 px.

## 3. Page

- The page is a `.page` div sized to the document's real proportions (A4
  portrait 794×1123 px, A4 landscape, or the source's own canvas — e.g. a
  citizenship card 1200×815 px, scaled with `transform: scale()` to fit A4).
- **No border on the page div or document edge.** The document has no outer
  frame; borders belong to the elements inside (boxes, tables, stamps) where
  the source shows them.
- Content-driven height: use `height: auto` or `min-height` so the page grows
  with content; never clip.
- Print rules every file carries:

```css
@page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 0; }
@media print {
  body { background: #ffffff !important; margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; }
  .page {
    margin: 0 !important;
    box-shadow: none !important;
    page-break-after: always;
  }
  .no-print { display: none !important; }
}
```
- A4 portrait pages additionally set `.page { width: 210mm; height: auto; }`
  inside the print block.

## 4. Element replacement

Nothing from the scan is embedded — every photo, seal, stamp, signature,
thumb impression, and QR becomes a bordered box (or circle) of the same size
and position, labelled:

| Source element | Replacement | Label |
|---|---|---|
| Photograph | solid-border box, same size | `Photograph Sd.` |
| Coat of Arms / logo | solid-border box or circle | `Coat of Arms of Nepal` |
| Round office seal | circle (`border-radius: 50%`) | `Round Office Seal` |
| Thumb impression | dashed-border box | `Provided` (or `Right` / `Left`) |
| Signature area | solid-border box | `[Role] Signature` |
| Signature inline | text | `Sd.` |
| QR code | solid-border square | `QR Code` |

- Stamp and photo boxes match the source's dimensions and placement exactly.
- Handwritten-looking or variable data becomes the box label text itself when
  there is no clearer value.

## 5. Editable fields

- Every value that could vary per document: `contenteditable="true"` plus
  `data-field="snake_case_name"`. Labels and structural text are not editable.
- Repeated structures use dot notation: `items.0.rate`, `plots.1.area`.
- Include the hover/focus styles for editable fields:

```css
[contenteditable="true"]:hover { outline: 2px dashed #000000; cursor: text; }
[contenteditable="true"]:focus { outline: 2px solid #000000; background: #ffffff; }
```

## 6. Output format

- One standalone HTML file: `<!DOCTYPE html>`, `<html lang="en">`,
  `<meta charset="UTF-8">`, descriptive `<title>`.
- All CSS in one `<style>` block or `style=` attributes. No `<img>`, no
  scripts, no web fonts, no external requests — renders identically offline.

## 7. Conventions from finished work

The reference snippets in the other file are the strongest signal — the same
hand that will clean your draft wrote them. When your situation matches a
snippet, reuse its pattern exactly: same page sizing approach, same box
styles, same field markup, same table construction. When it does not match,
follow these rules and imitate the snippets' spirit.

## 8. Task

Digitize the source document in the image into one standalone HTML file per
the rules above, imitating the reference snippets' conventions. Output only
the HTML — no markdown fences, no commentary.
